# **📌 Slide 31 — Nested If-Else**  
fileciteturn0file0

### **What is Nested If-Else?**
You put an **if / if-else inside another if / else block**.

Use it when:
- You need **multiple levels of decision-making**
- One condition depends on another

### **General Syntax (from slide):**
```c
if (expression1) {
    if (expression2) {
        // inner-if
    }
    else {
        // inner-else
    }
}
else {
    if (expression3) {
        // inner-if
    }
    else {
        // inner-else
    }
}
```

### **Exam Tip:**
Nested if-else is useful when solving **range-based** or **category** questions.

---

# **📌 Slide 32 — Nested If-Else Program Example**  
fileciteturn0file0

The slide contains this code:

```c
#include<stdio.h>
int main() {
    int num = 1;
    if (num < 10) {
        if (num == 1) {
            printf("The value is:%d\n", num);
        }
        else {
            printf("The value is greater than 1");
        }
    }
    else {
        printf("The value is greater than 10");
    }
    return 0;
}
```

### **Program Output:**
```
The value is:1
```

### **Why?**
- num = 1  
- `num < 10` → true  
- `num == 1` → true  

So inner-if runs.

### **Concept Highlight:**
First condition narrows the range, inner conditions refine the decision.

